{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CetvkC8hPqbJd38S7fRRF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The suite was failing because of a real concurrency bug in `Tee`/`TeePeer.__anext__` in `asyncstdlib/itertools.py`, not a bad test — I fixed it rather than deleting/skipping the test, since that would have hidden a genuine correctness bug in the library's core `tee()` primitive.\n\n**The bug:** when multiple tee peers concurrently found the shared buffer's frontier node empty (the documented \"no lock needed if the source is concurrency-safe\" case), each independently called the underlying iterator and blindly overwrote the same shared node. This silently dropped items and forked peers onto disconnected buffer chains — able to cause missing items or even hangs in concurrent consumers of `tee()`.\n\n**The fix:** peers now append their fetched value to whatever is currently the shared frontier at completion time (not the possibly-stale node they originally captured), and if another peer already filled their original slot, they donate their own fetch as a queued-ahead value instead of losing it. I kept the original \"recheck after acquiring the lock\" logic so a real user-supplied lock still avoids redundant fetches.\n\nAll 394 tests pass, consistently across 5 repeated runs (this was a deterministic bug, not flakiness)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":253,"cache_read_input_tokens":91567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":253},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30c4eb48-66c5-4fe0-997f-94aeaa07e90d","uuid":"6cd2774c-d804-4735-bf88-477a63c62a4a","timestamp":"2026-09-10T01:56:09.139Z","request_id":"req_011CetvkBUzsPef892tMt86X"}
